    "problem_statement": "### Description\n\nIt seems there's an issue with the configuration of allowed truthy values in the `truthy` rule. The recent changes have led to a `NameError` being raised due to an undefined variable `TRUTHY`. This error occurs across multiple modules, causing a significant disruption in functionality.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe `truthy` rule should correctly recognize and handle the allowed truthy values without raising any errors. The configuration should be robust enough to prevent such undefined variable issues.\n\n### How to Reproduce\n\nTo reproduce the issue, you can attempt to lint a YAML file with the following configuration:\n\n```yaml\ntruthy:\n  allowed-values: ['true', 'false']\n  check-keys: true\n```\n\nAttempting to lint any YAML file with this configuration will result in a `NameError` due to the undefined `TRUTHY` variable. The error message will indicate that `TRUTHY` is not defined, halting the linting process.\n\n### Versions\n\n- Python 3.10.15\n- Operating System: Linux\n- Linter Version: [Specify the version if known]\n\nThis issue is critical as it affects the core functionality of the linter, preventing it from processing YAML files correctly."
